Databricks uses Apache Spark to process massive data efficiently.


**Challenges with the Traditional data platforms**

	1.multiple tools
	(ingestion, processing, orcestration,goverance)
	was very hard to integrate so many tools

	2.complex infrstructure
	need to manage cluster manualy,very defficult to scale and maintain

	 3.Slow & inefficient pipeline
	 traditional etl piplelines are slow

	4.Lack of  collabration
	Teams end up working in isolation, sharing the notebooks(jupyeter noteebook)/code is painfull

	5.Unrealiable data lakes
     Datalake provides flexibility , also hold huge data -- used by DS/ML team
     Datawarehouse is more performant or relaiabe -- Used by BI/reporting team
     In the above data from DataLake is sent to Datawarehouse
     Datawarehouse holds subset of DataLake

     In traditional systesm 2 different systesm has to be maintained
     extra ETL activity required to bring data from Datalake to Datawarehouse
     Here the challenge is same copy at 2 different loc (Datalake & Datwarehouse)

	In traditional Datalake No ACID transactions.
	Also schema mismatches can break the pipeline
	In traditional Data lake there is no versioning
	There is no audit histroy

	6.No Vendor locking



In Databricks

Ingestion  -> lake flow connect
ETL - Lake flow declarative pipeline (Delta live tables)
Orchestration - Lake flow jobs
Governance - Unity catalog


Databricks offers Data Lake house, it is powered by Delta Lake

 Data Lake  ( eg: AWS S3 / ADLS Gen2,GCP)
on top of this cloud data, Databricks will create a wrapper and provide Delta Lake
This Delta Lake is combination of Data Lake + Data warehouse
Data is still kept in our cloud, Data bricks just creates a wrapper on it.
Delta lake provides
	Acid transactions
	Time travel
	Schema enforcement


**--Read bottom to up--**
Unity Catalog -  Governance/Metadata
Delta Lake
Cloud storage - Azure/AWS/GCP -- Data Lake

